# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the context root's,
# and the root one is written for the runtime image: it excludes requirements/
# dev.txt, tests/ and scripts/, all of which this image needs. Without this file
# the build fails on a missing dev.txt.
#
# The image carries dependencies only — run_layout_docker.sh mounts the working
# tree over /app — so everything but requirements/ is excluded, which keeps the
# context at a few kilobytes.
*
!requirements/
